{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And this</b> — He returns to explain what the war is that HaShem will wage against the nations that exiled half the city into captivity." "<b>He shall rot</b> — a verb from the heavy binyan. Every word that comes in the pa'el tongue [Aramaic active], and every word that comes in the sh'var tongue [Aramaic passive], is called the dagesh binyan." "<b>They shall rot</b> — from the nif'al binyan, and both are from doubled-root [פעלי הכפל] roots. And the proof: 'they shall rot in their iniquity' [like]: 'and his bonds melted' [מס, same root]."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {2 "The verse cited as proof, ימקו בעונם, does not appear in the biblical canon as such; it may be a paraphrase or a citation from a non-canonical source. וימסו אסוריו echoes Judges 15:14 or similar phrasing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:06.255634356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}